seg-c51dc64d4184 = Work done for you, on your system: the paid custom study, not the free <c1/> command.

# text
seg-8be27ff259ec = Why a custom study

# text
seg-e8518d0cf698 = When the question is yours but the time, the modelling or the clearance is not: we model your system with the same engine, label every figure Validated or Modelled, and hand back a result you can reproduce.

# text
seg-baa471fe1dfd = Programme and procurement teams who need an independent, modelled view of a PNT (positioning, navigation and timing) architecture's resilience

# text
seg-fa35052e3cca = Hardware builders who want models of their own devices

# text
seg-2de5d196de8d = Export-sensitive programmes, and teams who want Kshana in their toolchain

# text
seg-ed788268ba39 = A Modelled PNT-resilience study, for example an optimism-gap audit. Not a certification.

# text
seg-e030d9e40ff2 = Sensor and resilience models calibrated to your hardware

# text
seg-ad170a69d508 = Export-controlled resilience work under the appropriate clearance and NDA (non-disclosure agreement)

# text
seg-4d8a03851089 = Commercial support and integration, training and consulting

# text
seg-23723d311433 = Scoped to your question and delivered under contract, reproducible from scenario, seed and engine version.

# text
seg-164d0c3f0427 = One engine, two licences.

# text
seg-fcdf1186bc1d = Pick the one that fits how you use it. Both cover the same open engine; nothing is held back from either.

